        <!--
            Marker protocols — Sendable / Copyable / Escapable / SendableMetatype.

            These four are compile-time-only protocols: Swift emits no witness table
            and no concrete conformance descriptor in TBD, so the
            HandleConformance path returns a TypeConformance with an empty descriptor
            symbol. The typedb entry is needed so that classes / structs / enums (and
            in particular actor types) which list these in their `conformances` array
            can resolve a real TypeRecord during lookup — without it, downstream
            ShouldEmitConformance silently drops every marker conformance because
            TryGetTypeRecord fails.

